oice commands will always be recognized or executed as intended.\n\n6. Maps and Location Information: Maps, routes, coordinates, nearby locations, travel information, and other location-based features may depend on Apple Maps, device positioning, network connectivity, and third-party information. The accuracy, completeness, availability, and timeliness of this information may vary. Routes and travel information may not reflect current road conditions, closures, restrictions, or other relevant circumstances. Always verify important information and follow applicable traffic rules, signs, and safety instructions.\n\n7. Loyalty Cards, Tickets, Logos, Barcodes, and QR Codes: Loyalty cards, tickets, logos, barcode information, QR codes, generated barcodes, scanned barcodes, and related images are stored and displayed for user convenience. Their validity, accuracy, readability, acceptance, and compatibility with stores, scanners, ticketing systems, payment systems, or third-party services are not guaranteed. The App does not issue or validate the underlying cards or tickets unless expressly stated for a specific feature. You remain responsible for verifying that stored information is valid and can be used by the relevant issuer or service.\n\n8. Vault and Stored Information: The Vault allows you to store information such as usernames, email addresses, passwords, websites, PIN codes, OTP secrets, notes, tags, favorites, custom secrets, password expiration dates, and other supported content. A Vault item may contain multiple custom secrets with labels defined by you.\n\nPasswords, PIN codes, OTP secrets, and custom secret values stored in the Vault are encrypted using AES-GCM. Descriptive information, including titles, categories, usernames, email addresses, websites, notes, and tags, is not encrypted by this Vault encryption. Accordingly, you should not assume that all information associated with a Vault item is encrypted.\n\nEncryption reduces the risk of unauthorized access but cannot guarantee absolute security. The security of stored information may also depend on device security, operating system protections, access controls, backups, and the absence of malware or unauthorized modifications to the device. Rooted, jailbroken, compromised, or otherwise insecure devices may expose information to additional risks. You are responsible for protecting your device, Apple Account, device passcode, and access to the Vault. Nothing in this section excludes any security or data-protection obligations that apply to the developer under mandatory law.\n\n9. Device Authentication and Biometrics: Access to the Vault may use Face ID, Touch ID, the device passcode, or other authentication mechanisms provided by the operating system. Individual Vault items may optionally require biometric authentication even after the Vault has been unlocked. Biometric authentication is performed through the operating system and supported device hardware. The App does not receive, store, or transmit biometric information. Availability and operation depend on device hardware, operating system support, permissions, and user configuration. You should maintain an appropriate device passcode and understand the authentication settings configured on your device.\n\n10. Password Generator, Clipboard, and AutoFill: Password generation, password visibility controls, automatic Vault locking, clipboard auto-clearing, and AutoFill features are provided to assist with password management. Generated passwords are created locally on the device. You are responsible for choosing appropriate passwords, storing them securely, and ensuring that they meet the requirements of the services where they are used. Clipboard contents may remain accessible temporarily according to operating system behavior until automatically cleared or manually removed. The App cannot guarantee that clipboard contents will be cleared at a particular time or that other applications will not access clipboard data